| [`docs/hardening-security.md`](../../docs/hardening-security.md) | Before open beta launch; after auth, RLS, publish, or upload changes | Walk the security checklist; run lint, build, E2E, `db:status` |
| [`docs/qa-mobile.md`](../../docs/qa-mobile.md) | Before shipping editor/marketing/public-invite polish; after layout or image changes | Manual pass on 360px + real phone; same commands as below |
| [`docs/add-template.md`](../../docs/add-template.md) | When you add template #2 or #3 from your designs | Follow scaffold → theme → registry → preview wiring checklist |

**Typical command flow (most tasks):**

```bash
npm run lint
npm run build
npx playwright install chromium   # first time only (or after Playwright upgrade)
npm run test:e2e                  # all smoke tests
npm run test:e2e -- --project=mobile-chrome   # mobile viewport only
npm run db:status                 # confirm Supabase migrations applied
```

**Optional authenticated E2E** (create draft → editor) — set in shell or CI secrets:

```bash
PLAYWRIGHT_TEST_EMAIL="your-test-user@example.com"
PLAYWRIGHT_TEST_PASSWORD="your-password"
npm run test:e2e
```

**Supabase migration** (e.g. drop `rsvps` table) — apply linked project migrations, not only the SQL file in git:

```bash
npm run db:push
```

